          "text": "<teammate-message teammate_id=\"team-lead\">\nImplement release-plan Task 8 (packed non-workspace consumer) for storyproof, plus a small prerequisite. Repo: /home/leon0399/Projects/storyproof (pnpm workspace: packages/storyproof + apps/website). The local checkout is on `main`, verified in sync with origin at commit `eedad1d` (\"chore(storyproof): replace bespoke build/pack/verify scripts with conventional tooling (#1)\") — branch from there and confirm that SHA is your base before starting; if it isn't, stop and report. **All work goes through a PR — never push to main. Never merge. Never git stash/reset/checkout--.**\n\nRead first: root AGENTS.md, packages/storyproof/AGENTS.md, .github/workflows/ci.yml, packages/storyproof/package.json, tsdown.config.ts, packages/storyproof/playwright.config.ts, packages/storyproof/test/acceptance/addon-suite.ts, packages/storyproof/test/fixtures/project/**, packages/storyproof/src/preset.ts, and Task 8 + the 2026-07-26/27 deviation notes in packages/storyproof/docs/2026-07-24-public-preview-release-plan.md.\n\n## Design (decided by the owner — implement this, don't redesign)\n\n**Overriding principle: NO bespoke scripts.** This project spent a full session deleting seven `scripts/*.mjs` files in favor of conventional tooling. The harness is *workflow steps + package.json scripts*, nothing else. If you find yourself writing a `.mjs` orchestrator, stop and report instead.\n\n### Commit 1 (separate, first): tsdown `exports: true`\n\ntsdown can generate `package.json`'s `exports` field from its `entry` list (verified present in tsdown 0.22.14's types: `exports?: WithEnabled<ExportsOptions>`). Today the four entry points are hand-duplicated across `tsdown.config.ts` `entry`, `package.json` `exports`, and the test allowlist.\n\nEnable it, then **empirically verify the generated `exports` map is byte-identical in behavior to the current hand-authored one** — the package is already published at `0.0.1-alpha.1`, so a silent contract change is unacceptable. Diff the generated `package.json` against the committed one and report exactly what changed. If tsdown's output differs in any way that changes resolution (different condition order, added/removed conditions, added `./package.json` export, etc.), STOP and report rather than accepting it. Keep `test/pack-inventory.test.ts` passing (it asserts the four entries ship). Also ensure `git diff --exit-code` in CI won't trip: if tsdown rewrites package.json during build, that's a tracked-file mutation — decide and report how it interacts with the `package` job's clean-tree check (this is a real risk; if it can't be resolved cleanly, revert commit 1 and report why).\n\n### Commits 2+: the consumer examples and CI\n\n**Examples** (root `examples/`, NOT pnpm-workspace members — confirm they're excluded so a workspace link is impossible):\n- `examples/react-vite-sb10.5` — canonical, `@storybook/react-vite` + `storybook` pinned `~10.5.0`\n- `examples/react-vite-sb10.0` — supported floor, pinned `~10.0.0`\n- `examples/nextjs-vite-sb10.5` — `@storybook/nextjs-vite`, pinned `~10.5.0`\n\nEach is a **standalone, human-readable Storybook quickstart**: own package.json (explicit deps, no `workspace:`/`catalog:`/relative-path refs), `.storybook/main.ts` registering `storyproof` via the package export (`storyproof/preset` or the addons array — match how a real consumer would), a couple of simple deterministic stories, and a short README. Someone must be able to clone the repo, `cd` into one, install, and run it. They depend on `storyproof` at its published version; CI overlays the packed tarball on top.\n\nDirectory names carry the SB minor deliberately, and the `~` pins keep the name honest — do not use `^` ranges.\n\n**Acceptance tests stay in one place.** Do NOT copy test infra into the examples (that would break their standalone-quickstart quality and duplicate the spec). The existing reusable `test/acceptance/addon-suite.ts` is the spec — run Playwright *from packages/storyproof* against an example's dev server, parameterized by env var (e.g. an example-directory/URL env the existing `playwright.config.ts` webServer block reads). Extend the existing config minimally; keep the current fixture-project flow working unchanged.\n\n**CI: one new job in the existing `.github/workflows/ci.yml`** (not a separate workflow):\n- Restore the `package` job's `upload-artifact` step (removed earlier because nothing consumed it — now this job does).\n- New `consumer` job: `needs: package`, `strategy.matrix.example: [react-vite-sb10.5, react-vite-sb10.0, nextjs-vite-sb10.5]`, `fail-fast: false`, single Node version (the `.node-version` floor — Node coverage is already proven by other jobs; do NOT make this a 2D matrix).\n- Steps, roughly: checkout → pnpm/node setup → `download-artifact` the tarball → install in `examples/${{ matrix.example }}` → `pnpm add file:<absolute tarball path>` → assert the resolved storyproof lives under that example's `node_modules` (one cheap check, not an elaborate negative-control fixture) → `playwright install --with-deps chromium` → run the acceptance suite against that example → upload the Playwright report on failure.\n- Actions stay SHA-pinned exactly as the existing ones are. `actionlint` and `zizmor .github/workflows/` must both be clean.\n\n**Known unknown to verify, not guess:** `pnpm install` inside a non-workspace-member directory under a workspace root may need `--ignore-workspace` (the deleted `test-exports.mjs` used it). Determine empirically what's actually required and use the minimum.\n\n**Scope discipline:** the acceptance suite runs in full in every cell — no smoke/full tiering, no test tagging. Do not add Verdaccio, pkg.pr.new, or a local registry. Do not add Node-version or Next-version dimensions.\n\n## Verification (record every exit code honestly; redirect long output to files under /tmp/claude-1000/-home-leon0399-Projects-llame/a398f1c1-a27d-4c74-8f62-94c24993161f/tasks/ and read the files — never pipe to head/grep)\n\nLocal: `pnpm install`, `pnpm --filter storyproof build`, `pnpm --filter storyproof test`, `typecheck`, `lint`, `pnpm format:check`, `actionlint`, `zizmor .github/workflows/`, and a real `pnpm pack` + `pnpm add file:` install into one example to prove the install path works.\n\n**This WSL2 host cannot run Playwright** (missing browser system libraries) — so the browser acceptance runs are CI-only. Say so plainly in the PR body; do not claim you ran them. Expect to iterate against CI: push, watch `gh run watch <id> --repo leon0399/storyproof --exit-status`, read failures, fix, repeat. That's the expected loop for this task — budget for several rounds.\n\n## Docs (same PR)\n\nTick Task 8's checkboxes in the release plan with a dated deviation note recording the actual design (examples-as-fixtures with version-suffixed names, workflow-steps-as-harness with no orchestrator script, artifact reuse from the `package` job, no smoke/full tiering, no negative-control fixture) and *why* it differs from the plan's original `test/fixtures/consumer/` + `test:consumer` sketch. Update root ROADMAP.md (P0/P1 bullets this completes), the package `CHANGELOG.md` `[Unreleased]` section (Keep a Changelog format), root AGENTS.md (the examples/ layout + how to run one locally), and packages/storyproof/AGENTS.md if its commands change. Prettier-write only files you touched.\n\n## PR\n\nConventional commits with these trailers on each:\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011apGNwN6NEjPRtHLkX4YPF\n\nNon-draft PR against main via `gh pr create --body-file`, ending with:\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_011apGNwN6NEjPRtHLkX4YPF\n\nNo \"Test plan\" section. Report back: PR URL, the exports:true diff outcome (critical), what `--ignore-workspace` turned out to require, per-job CI results, how many CI rounds it took, and anything you're uncertain about.\n</teammate-message>",
